[des@yatton.inmos.co.uk (David Shepherd) notes:]
>When wearing a ring of teleportation I attacked a floating eye and
>got frozen by its gaze. I then started to teleport, still frozen.
>1) should you still be frozen by the gaze when you've teleported?
.
the sequence is you are frozen by the 1st gaze of the floating eye. so now
you are frozen for N moves regardless of what happens next ... i.e. you or
the eye could wander off, doesn't matter.
>2) if you then happen to land in a shop should you be able to pick up
>   what you land on -- what happened was I landed in the shop, automatically
>   picked up what I landed on, then while still frozen got teleported out
>   of the shop and rapidly got killed by a bunch of Kops.
.
okay, you've been frozen because you, sort of, blindly attacked the eye
(hint!). you've got your auto-magic pickup option set to true (i'd
suggest turning this off, perhaps using the "@" command, and then
turning it on discriminately). the auto-magic pickup is just that
whether you're blind, frozen, whatever. your demise was inevitable
(and predictable). some strategy tips:
1) never fight a floating eye eye-to-eye! kicking it isn't great either.
2) never have your auto-magic pickup on when you can't control your
    teleports! better yet, never have "pickup on" unless you know
    specifically what you want to pickup and can therefore save yourself
    a move by having "pickup on".
.
>I suggested you should be able to move as soon as you can no longer
>see the eye (i.e. get teleported away).
.
it's now agreed that one look was all it took ...
.
>you should not be able to pick objects up when frozen.
.
that's completely (optionally) under your control.

